### Defining a Custom ActionType in Elasticsearch (Java)

Source: https://context7.com/elastic/elasticsearch/llms.txt

This class defines a unique `ActionType` for the custom action within Elasticsearch. It assigns a unique name and specifies the `ActionResponse` class associated with this action, enabling Elasticsearch to properly route and handle the custom operation.

```java
// Define custom action type
public class CustomAction extends ActionType<CustomResponse> {
    public static final CustomAction INSTANCE = new CustomAction();
    public static final String NAME = "cluster:admin/custom_action";

    private CustomAction() {
        super(NAME, CustomResponse::new);
    }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Creating a Custom Action Request for Elasticsearch (Java)

Source: https://context7.com/elastic/elasticsearch/llms.txt

This Java class represents the custom request object for the Elasticsearch action. It extends `ActionRequest` to carry specific parameters, includes logic for stream serialization/deserialization for inter-node communication, and provides validation for input data.

```java
// Custom request
import org.elasticsearch.common.io.stream.StreamInput;
import org.elasticsearch.common.io.stream.StreamOutput;

public class CustomRequest extends ActionRequest {
    private String parameter;

    public CustomRequest(String parameter) {
        this.parameter = parameter;
    }

    public CustomRequest(StreamInput in) throws IOException {
        super(in);
        this.parameter = in.readString();
    }

    @Override
    public void writeTo(StreamOutput out) throws IOException {
        super.writeTo(out);
        out.writeString(parameter);
    }

    @Override
    public ActionRequestValidationException validate() {
        if (parameter == null || parameter.isEmpty()) {
            ActionRequestValidationException e = new ActionRequestValidationException();
            e.addValidationError("parameter must not be empty");
            return e;
        }
        return null;
    }

    public String getParameter() {
        return parameter;
    }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Process Custom Elasticsearch REST Request (Java)

Source: https://context7.com/elastic/elasticsearch/llms.txt

This Java method demonstrates how to implement a `prepareRequest` handler for a custom Elasticsearch REST endpoint. It extracts parameters from the request URL or body, creates a custom request object, and uses the client to execute a custom action, returning a listener for the channel. This allows for custom API endpoint behavior.

```java
protected RestChannelConsumer prepareRequest(RestRequest request, NodeClient client) {
        String param = request.param("param");
        if (param == null) {
            param = request.content().utf8ToString();
        }

        CustomRequest customRequest = new CustomRequest(param);

        return channel -> client.execute(
            CustomAction.INSTANCE,
            customRequest,
            new RestToXContentListener<>(channel)
        );
    }
```

