### Handling Custom Action Business Logic in Elasticsearch (Java)

Source: https://context7.com/elastic/elasticsearch/llms.txt

This `TransportCustomAction` class implements the server-side business logic for the custom action. Extending `HandledTransportAction`, it receives `CustomRequest` objects, performs an operation (e.g., `processRequest`), and returns a `CustomResponse` asynchronously via an `ActionListener`.

```java
// Transport action implementation
import org.elasticsearch.action.support.HandledTransportAction;
import org.elasticsearch.common.inject.Inject;
import org.elasticsearch.tasks.Task;
import org.elasticsearch.transport.TransportService;

public class TransportCustomAction extends HandledTransportAction<CustomRequest, CustomResponse> {

    @Inject
    public TransportCustomAction(TransportService transportService, ActionFilters actionFilters) {
        super(CustomAction.NAME, transportService, actionFilters, CustomRequest::new);
    }

    @Override
    protected void doExecute(Task task, CustomRequest request, ActionListener<CustomResponse> listener) {
        try {
            // Perform custom logic
            String result = processRequest(request.getParameter());
            listener.onResponse(new CustomResponse(result));
        } catch (Exception e) {
            listener.onFailure(e);
        }
    }

    private String processRequest(String parameter) {
        // Custom business logic
        return "Processed: " + parameter;
    }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Creating a Custom Action Request for Elasticsearch (Java)

Source: https://context7.com/elastic/elasticsearch/llms.txt

This Java class represents the custom request object for the Elasticsearch action. It extends `ActionRequest` to carry specific parameters, includes logic for stream serialization/deserialization for inter-node communication, and provides validation for input data.

```java
// Custom request
import org.elasticsearch.common.io.stream.StreamInput;
import org.elasticsearch.common.io.stream.StreamOutput;

public class CustomRequest extends ActionRequest {
    private String parameter;

    public CustomRequest(String parameter) {
        this.parameter = parameter;
    }

    public CustomRequest(StreamInput in) throws IOException {
        super(in);
        this.parameter = in.readString();
    }

    @Override
    public void writeTo(StreamOutput out) throws IOException {
        super.writeTo(out);
        out.writeString(parameter);
    }

    @Override
    public ActionRequestValidationException validate() {
        if (parameter == null || parameter.isEmpty()) {
            ActionRequestValidationException e = new ActionRequestValidationException();
            e.addValidationError("parameter must not be empty");
            return e;
        }
        return null;
    }

    public String getParameter() {
        return parameter;
    }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Implementing a Custom Action Response for Elasticsearch (Java)

Source: https://context7.com/elastic/elasticsearch/llms.txt

This class defines the custom response object for the Elasticsearch action. It extends `ActionResponse` to encapsulate the result of the action, handling serialization for transport across nodes and `ToXContentObject` for proper JSON serialization in REST API responses.

```java
// Custom response
public class CustomResponse extends ActionResponse implements ToXContentObject {
    private String result;

    public CustomResponse(String result) {
        this.result = result;
    }

    public CustomResponse(StreamInput in) throws IOException {
        super(in);
        this.result = in.readString();
    }

    @Override
    public void writeTo(StreamOutput out) throws IOException {
        out.writeString(result);
    }

    @Override
    public XContentBuilder toXContent(XContentBuilder builder, Params params) throws IOException {
        builder.startObject();
        builder.field("result", result);
        builder.endObject();
        return builder;
    }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Registering Custom Actions and REST Handlers in Elasticsearch Plugin (Java)

Source: https://context7.com/elastic/elasticsearch/llms.txt

This Java class defines the main plugin entry point for an Elasticsearch custom action. It implements `ActionPlugin` to register custom `ActionHandler` instances (linking actions to transport implementations) and `RestHandler` instances, making custom REST endpoints available.

```java
import org.elasticsearch.plugins.ActionPlugin;
import org.elasticsearch.plugins.Plugin;
import org.elasticsearch.rest.RestHandler;
import org.elasticsearch.action.ActionRequest;
import org.elasticsearch.action.ActionResponse;
import org.elasticsearch.action.ActionType;
import org.elasticsearch.client.internal.node.NodeClient;
import org.elasticsearch.rest.BaseRestHandler;
import org.elasticsearch.rest.RestRequest;

import java.util.List;
import java.util.function.Supplier;

// Main plugin class
public class CustomActionPlugin extends Plugin implements ActionPlugin {

    @Override
    public List<ActionHandler<? extends ActionRequest, ? extends ActionResponse>> getActions() {
        return List.of(
            new ActionHandler<>(CustomAction.INSTANCE, TransportCustomAction.class)
        );
    }

    @Override
    public List<RestHandler> getRestHandlers(
        Settings settings,
        RestController restController,
        ClusterSettings clusterSettings,
        IndexScopedSettings indexScopedSettings,
        SettingsFilter settingsFilter,
        IndexNameExpressionResolver indexNameExpressionResolver,
        Supplier<DiscoveryNodes> nodesInCluster
    ) {
        return List.of(new RestCustomAction());
    }
}
```

Source: https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/main/docs/internal/GeneralArchitectureGuide.md

Action invocation: - [TransportMasterNodeAction]: Executes an action on the master node. Typically used to perform cluster state updates, as these can only
be performed on the master. The base class contains logic for locating the master node and delegating to it to execute the specified logic.
- [TransportNodesAction]: Executes an action on many nodes then collates the responses.
- [TransportLocalClusterStateAction]: Waits for a cluster state that optionally meets some criteria and performs a read action on it on the
coordinating node.
- [TransportReplicationAction]: Execute an action on a primary shard followed by all replicas that exist for that shard. The base class
implements logic for locating the primary and replica shards in the cluster and delegating to the relevant nodes. Often used for index
updates in stateful Elasticsearch.
- [TransportSingleShardAction]: Executes a read operation on a specific shard, the base class contains logic for locating an available copy
of the nominated shard and delegating to the relevant node to execute the action. On a failure, the action is retried on a different copy.

